Third-party attributions
------------------------

PJRT / OpenXLA C API (https://github.com/openxla/xla), Apache License 2.0. The
reference design for the plugin boundary: a versioned C API with opaque
client, compiled-executable and buffer handles, which is the same shape as the
Strata plugin vtable. PJRT is *not* copied or linked in Phase B1. Whether
Strata adopts the PJRT C API wholesale or defines a smaller vtable of its own
is an open decision recorded in docs/design-notes.md; if PJRT is adopted, its
license and notice will be added here.

CubeCL (https://github.com/tracel-ai/burn), MIT License, Copyright (c) The Burn
Authors. The closest existing design to Strata's goals, and the intended
portable GPU backend in Phase B1. Referenced for its trait boundaries and
compile/runtime split. No CubeCL source is copied; it is consumed as a
dependency under its own license.

Burn (https://github.com/tracel-ai/burn), MIT License, Copyright (c) The Burn
Authors. Its separation of a device-execution trait from a graph-compilation
trait is the closest prior art for Strata's subgraph-level vendor interface, and
is the main input to the interface design. No Burn source is copied.

cutile-rs (https://crates.io/crates/cutile-rs) and cuda-oxide
(https://github.com/NVIDIA/cuda-rust), NVIDIA. Evaluated as optional tuned
NVIDIA backends (Phases B3 and later). Not depended upon in Phase B1; cutile-rs
is expected to be consumed as a published crate under its own license, and
cuda-oxide is nightly-pinned and isolated behind an optional crate.
